preConditionHook:
// THE MOVING AVERAGE IS THE MINIMUM TARGET OF A COUNTERTREND SCALP. Brooks
// states it twice (Ranges ch6 on gaps, Trends ch10 on second entries): a
// countertrend long taken below the average is expected to reach the average,
// so that is where the scalp comes off. The test is on the bar's high against
// the EMA, not on the close, and it is position-gated.
//
// toleranceTicks takes the exit that many ticks SHORT of the average. Ticks
// division-first, ctx.MinMove() / ctx.PriceScale() computed once into tickSz;
// both are per-symbol constants (VERIFIED, one change print per chart, at
// bar 1).
//
// THE PLACEMENT TRAP, recorded by the source and not fixed here: the rule is
// written for a long entered BELOW the average, so a long entered above it
// exits on its first bar. A placement concern, not a change to the condition.
//
// EMA MIRROR: MultiWalk's WFSafe_Xaverage, which the EasyLanguage twin calls.
// MEASURED bit-identical to the plain XAverage built-in at a fixed length
// (EL_XAverage_Probe.txt, @OJ 240min, 17,785 bars).
//   * SEED: the PRICE on the study's first calculated bar (ctx.CurrentBar()
//     == 1), NOT a length-term simple average -- the textbook twin was still
//     3.4e-05 off at bar 100.
//   * ONE STATEMENT, IN EL'S FORM: x + sf*(p - x), not sf*p + (1-sf)*x; the
//     two separate on 67% of bars past 100 and XAverage tracks the first.
//   * NO WARM-UP HOLE: non-zero from bar 1, so no bar-count guard returning 0.
//   * LENGTH CHANGE MEASURED (2026-09-17): the wrapper recomputes SF on the
//     bar the length changes and carries its state, so emaLength MAY be
//     optimized in grids.
// This rule reads the CURRENT value only, so no history buffer and no lagged
// read.
//
// Not CloseAboveAverage, an ENTRY comparing the close with its own SIMPLE
// average. Not EmaTouch, an Entry, direction-agnostic, asking whether the bar
// STRADDLES the average; this asks, in the exit pane, whether the bar reached
// it from one side. Not CloseWithinAtrOfEma, a symmetric ATR band.
// Scratch below is declared in localVariables, not at hook scope: the
// generator only prefixes declared locals, so a hook-scope declaration
// is a redefinition when this rule is placed twice in one strategy.
// Every one is fully assigned each bar before it is read.
tickSz = ctx.MinMove() / ctx.PriceScale();
emaSf = 2.0 / (emaLength + 1.0);
if (ctx.CurrentBar() == 1) {
    emaVal = close[0];
} else {
    emaVal = emaVal + emaSf * (close[0] - emaVal);
}
